  "done": [
   "Blocker 1 (Attention/Horror read surface): WM-31 now names the reads from existing web.view members. Departure is pod_at == IN_FLIGHT with transit_state, leg_dir, leg_origin_id and leg_target_id. Arrival is pod_at == a record id with transit_state IDLE. Berthing is transit_state == BERTHING. Dormancy is nodes[].loaded, derived from the Graph's section().dormant, and a consumer may read section() directly. I chose existing members over adding one, so WM-36's field list and AC-WM-60's exact-list assertion stay true. Updated the POD_DEPARTED and DERELICT_LOADED/UNLOADED event rows, the Attention dependency row, WM-36 and AC-WM-60. WM-31 also argues that level reads cannot miss a departure or flip, since each state holds for at least 360 ticks.",
   "Blocker 2 (pod_arrived_seq / berthed_seq undefined): added a WM-31 rule block 'The Save/Load counters', choosing non-persisted host-local runtime counters over block fields. They are u32, start at 0 and increase by exactly 1. They are exposed through one separate pure read, web.save_seq() -> {pod_arrived_seq, berthed_seq}, granted to Save/Load's facet only. It sits beside web.leg_timing() and is not part of web.view. pod_arrived_seq increments in the pod_settle apply that sets POD_ARRIVED, and not in the failed settle of the T5 reversal. berthed_seq increments in the last berth_step apply that sets BERTHED, and never for UNBERTHED, web_reconcile or post_restore. Late applies still count exactly once. post_restore resets both to 0 and increments nothing, and Save/Load re-reads its last-seen values after a load (ADR-0006 1.12). This keeps the D.11 byte figures (machine_bytes 125, about 756 B), the golden save and state_hash unchanged.",
   "Propagated the counter rule to: WM-3 (derived/not-persisted sentence), WM-30 (Not persisted list), the POD_ARRIVED and BERTHED event rows, the D.11 Output Range note, AC-WM-57 (increment and restore cases), AC-WM-59 (counters absent from the golden save and hash row) and AC-WM-75 (no extra bytes or dirty keys). Every changed rule is marked '(Amended 2026-10-29 \u00e2\u20ac\u201d sync knock-on fix)'."
  ],
  "not_done": [
   {
    "blocker": "ADR-0004 (the Alternative 9 rejection text) writes the counters as 'web.view.pod_arrived_seq', and its Web Map rows say 'web.state counters'. ADR-0006 1.12 and OQ-K say 'web.state read-view members'. This GDD puts them on the separate read web.save_seq(), not on web.view.",
    "reason": "ADRs are outside my edit scope and the ruling is that ADRs win. The ADR wording is loose about which read surface carries the counters, and the Web Map ADR (OQ-K) is where it gets fixed. If the ADR needs them literally on web.view, WM-36 and AC-WM-60 must be extended and the Chart Table GDD's web.view field-list assertion revisited. I kept web.view unchanged so the Chart Table contract is untouched."
