    "where": "Dependencies table, Horror Entities row (L439) and the Bidirectional summary row (L975)",
    "issue": "Both rows still give the Horror interface as the events DERELICT_LOADED / DERELICT_UNLOADED and POD_DEPARTED. The fixer rewrote the Attention row (L431), but these rows were missed. WM-31 and the POD_DEPARTED and DERELICT_LOADED/UNLOADED event rows now say Horror does not subscribe and reads web.view (pod_at, transit_state, leg_dir, leg_origin_id, leg_target_id, nodes[].loaded) in its hook. An implementer of Horror would read two contradictory interface contracts for the very fix blocker 1 was about.",
